sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: Nick 2026-11-09, containers reach models with only the placeholder key and no real key on their Node (ADR 0252).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · `ai-router:model-forwarder NODE` on the Gateway, once per agent Node, and with `--remove` to withdraw it
  %% kind: ai_router.model_forwarder
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane R icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant R as Router Node<br/>services, over ssh
  participant N as Agent Node<br/>beast, over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit the forwarder<br/>the agent Node
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - renders the guard as `ai-router:task-guard` does, with the Node's WireGuard address added to its sources, or removed
  %%> - renders the forwarder's Caddyfile: the bridge address at port 8319, proxied unchanged to the guard origin; it holds no key
  %%> - pushes vault copies of the task key and the anchor key for the guard; the intent holds neither, and the forwarder gets neither
  %%> - takes the lock `ai_router_guard:<router Node>`, which guard runs share
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the ai-router extension is set up on its Node
  %%> - the Node is active Linux with a WireGuard address, and is neither the router's Node nor the swamp Node
  %%> - `--bridge` and `--address` name the container bridge and its IPv4 address; a removal reuses those of the last run
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>ai_router.model_forwarder
  SW->>R: Apply the guard<br/>Ansible
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the guard phase of `ai-router:task-guard`: keys, Caddyfile, unit, and the UFW allow of each forwarder Node above the deny
  %%> - its end checks: from the router Node and from the swamp Node, a source outside the admitted sources is refused
  SW->>N: Apply the forwarder<br/>Ansible
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks that the address belongs to the bridge
  %%> - runs its own Caddy, `orbit-ai-router-forwarder.service`, on the bridge address at port 8319: a dynamic user, no admin endpoint, no saved config, no key
  %%> - allows port 8319 in on the bridge only
  %%> - `--remove`: takes the unit, its folder and its UFW rule off the Node instead
  SW->>N: Prove the path<br/>from the agent Node
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - apply: a POST through the forwarder with no key gets the guard's 403, so the guard admits the Node and still demands the key
  %%> - remove: the guard port does not answer the Node
  alt the checks pass
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded
    Note over GW: Record the forwarder<br/>http://10.251.33.1:8319
    %%> Result:
    %%> - containers on the Node call this origin with the one task key; only the `agent` uid reaches it, by the container's own nftables rule
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
  end
